"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://westnorthants.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-05","committee":"Pensions Fund Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://westnorthants.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-12","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://westnorthants.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-13","committee":"Adult Social Care, Health and Communities Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://westnorthants.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-15","committee":"Place and Resources Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://westnorthants.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-19","committee":"Children, Education and Housing Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://westnorthants.moderngov.co.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-09-02","committee":"Place and Resources Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://westnorthants.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-07","committee":"Pensions Fund Committee - Investment Sub-Committee","time":"4.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://westnorthants.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-08","committee":"Children, Education and Housing Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://westnorthants.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-14","committee":"Planning Policy Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://westnorthants.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://westnorthants.moderngov.co.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Council releasing \u00a38.5m of \u00a310.1m contingency buffer to offset \u00a313.1m in-year overspend","lead":"Contingency depletion mid-year leaves the council exposed to further shocks in volatile demand-led services, particularly with six months remaining in the financial year.","iso":"2026-09-15","paper_title":"CLEAN WNC- Revenue Monitoring Report - 2026-27 - Period 4","paper_url":"https://westnorthants.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s30079/30079.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"\u00a33.4m of \u00a39.1m adult social care savings assessed as undeliverable as Sustainability Programme delays","lead":"When savings targets are not delivered, the council loses its primary tool for managing budget pressures and must instead rely on contingency or reserves, which are finite.","iso":"2026-09-15","paper_title":"CLEAN WNC- Revenue Monitoring Report - 2026-27 - Period 4","paper_url":"https://westnorthants.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s30079/30079.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Children's Trust overspend of \u00a318.7m reflecting unbudgeted placement surge in early 2026","lead":"Placement costs in a new contract are rising faster than anticipated, indicating either higher service need or market-driven inflation not captured in budget planning, and suggesting ongoing risk.","iso":"2026-09-15","paper_title":"CLEAN WNC- Revenue Monitoring Report - 2026-27 - Period 4","paper_url":"https://westnorthants.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s30079/30079.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-15","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"CLEAN WNC- Revenue Monitoring Report - 2026-27 - Period 4","paper_url":"https://westnorthants.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s30079/30079.pdf","headline":"Council releasing \u00a38.5m of \u00a310.1m contingency buffer to offset \u00a313.1m in-year overspend","detail":"The council set aside \u00a310.1m general contingency in 2026-27 budget to manage in-year risks. Period 4 forecast shows \u00a313.1m overspend with \u00a38.5m contingency released to offset it. Only \u00a31.6m remains held against pay award risk, effectively depleting contingency buffer mid-year. The \u00a31.3m MRP underspend provides some relief but does not restore contingency position.","category":"other","matters":"Contingency depletion mid-year leaves the council exposed to further shocks in volatile demand-led services, particularly with six months remaining in the financial year.","figures":"\u00a310.1m contingency set aside; \u00a38.5m released to offset overspend; \u00a31.6m retained for pay award; \u00a313.1m total forecast overspend; \u00a31.3m MRP underspend","quote":"Of this balance \u00a31.6m has been set aside to fund the additional forecast cost of the 2026-27 pay award, pending the outcome from current Trade Union consultation with members, whilst the remaining \u00a38.5m has been released into the position.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-15","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"CLEAN WNC- Revenue Monitoring Report - 2026-27 - Period 4","paper_url":"https://westnorthants.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s30079/30079.pdf","headline":"\u00a33.4m of \u00a39.1m adult social care savings assessed as undeliverable as Sustainability Programme delays","detail":"Adult Social Care is forecasting \u00a38.4m overspend, primarily driven by \u00a38.1m pressures in independent care sector. Of the \u00a39.1m savings required, \u00a33.4m is assessed undeliverable: \u00a31.9m from Sustainability Programme, \u00a30.8m from hospital discharge pathways review, and \u00a30.8m from direct payment packages review. The directorate cites timing of implementing changes, continued high demand, and prioritising the CQC Improvement Plan as factors reducing ability to realise planned savings.","category":"savings","matters":"When savings targets are not delivered, the council loses its primary tool for managing budget pressures and must instead rely on contingency or reserves, which are finite.","figures":"\u00a33.4m undeliverable out of \u00a39.1m (37% failure rate); \u00a31.9m Sustainability Programme; \u00a30.8m hospital discharge pathways; \u00a30.8m direct payments; \u00a38.4m total overspend; \u00a36.4m structural demand pressure; \u00a31.2m inflationary uplift","quote":"This is primarily due to the timing of implementing changes and achieving savings within the financial year, continued high demand for care services, and the need to prioritise delivery of the Care Quality Commission (CQC) Improvement Plan.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-15","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"CLEAN WNC- Revenue Monitoring Report - 2026-27 - Period 4","paper_url":"https://westnorthants.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s30079/30079.pdf","headline":"Children's Trust overspend of \u00a318.7m reflecting unbudgeted placement surge in early 2026","detail":"Northamptonshire Children's Trust is reporting a \u00a329.7m countywide overspend in its first year of operation. WNC's share based on the historical 55.84% split is \u00a316.6m. The placement overspend of \u00a315.6m reflects an unexpected significant increase in placements in early 2026 that was not anticipated in the current year contract sum. The council has made further provision of \u00a31.6m for potential deterioration due to ongoing demand risk, assessing this scenario as reasonable rather than remote given the pace of growth.","category":"demand","matters":"Placement costs in a new contract are rising faster than anticipated, indicating either higher service need or market-driven inflation not captured in budget planning, and suggesting ongoing risk.","figures":"\u00a318.7m WNC overspend; \u00a329.7m NCT countywide overspend; \u00a315.6m placement overspend; \u00a31.6m provision for deterioration; 55.84% WNC share; \u00a31.0m staffing overspend","quote":"NCT experienced a significant increase in placements, especially in the early part of the 2026 calendar year since the setting of the current year contract sum, which presents an immediate pressure in the 2026-27 financial year","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-15","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"CLEAN WNC- Revenue Monitoring Report - 2026-27 - Period 4","paper_url":"https://westnorthants.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s30079/30079.pdf","headline":"High Needs Block forecast to overspend by \u00a365.6m with cumulative deficit reaching \u00a370.7m by year-end","detail":"WNC has experienced an 88% increase in Education Health and Care Plans (EHCPs) since vesting day, larger than most councils nationally. Rising costs due to inflation and limited placement supply are driving an overall DSG overspend of \u00a365.2m. Although a \u00a349.9m High Needs Stability Grant will be received in Autumn 2026 to cover 90% of prior deficits, the in-year overspend means the cumulative deficit will reach \u00a370.7m by end of 2026-27, up from \u00a355.4m brought forward. The underlying high needs funding increase from prior year was only 0.5%, insufficient to address the structural gap.","category":"demand","matters":"A structural SEND funding gap that the temporary government stabilization grant will not solve means this deficit will continue to accumulate and potentially consume reserves.","figures":"88% increase in EHCPs since vesting; \u00a365.6m High Needs Block overspend; \u00a365.2m total DSG overspend; \u00a370.7m cumulative deficit expected by end 2026-27; \u00a355.4m brought forward; 0.5% prior year funding increase; lowest quartile nationally for per-pupil funding","quote":"WNC has seen an 88% increase in Education Health and Care Plans (EHCPs) since vesting day which is larger than most other councils nationally. In addition to this there are rising costs due to inflation, and current lack of placement supply in local state mainstream and special schools to meet demand and complexity, meaning that the Council has to resort to more expensive independent places.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-15","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix D - Forecast capital spend by scheme 2026-27","paper_url":"https://westnorthants.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s30053/30053.pdf","headline":"Significant capital programme underspend combined with budget removals","detail":"The approved capital programme of \u00a3122,968,479 is forecast to spend only \u00a3119,466,004. The council shows \u00a32,610,497 in underspend and is removing \u00a3834,426 of previously approved budget as no longer required. This represents \u00a33.4 million of capital not being deployed, with only \u00a31,161,210 carried forward to future years.","category":"capital","matters":"Inability to deploy planned capital combined with active budget removals signals either cash constraints or project delivery failures. This is a key indicator lenders use to assess financial discipline and forecast reliability.","figures":"Approved budget: \u00a3122,968,479; Forecast spend: \u00a3119,466,004; Underspend: \u00a32,610,497; Budget removals: \u00a3834,426; Carry forward: \u00a31,161,210","quote":"Total approved capital programme 122,968,479 119,466,004 - 1,161,210 - 2,610,497 834,426","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-15"},"name":"West Northamptonshire","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-17","since_iso":"2026-08-18","distress":false,"headline":"Council releasing \u00a38.5m of \u00a310.1m contingency buffer to offset \u00a313.1m in-year overspend","lead":"Contingency depletion mid-year leaves the council exposed to further shocks in volatile demand-led services, particularly with six months remaining in the financial year.","also":["41 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Audit and Governance Committee on 2026-09-23","n_findings":42,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"CLEAN WNC- Revenue Monitoring Report - 2026-27 - Period 4","top_paper_url":"https://westnorthants.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s30079/30079.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":123,"news_drafts_total":3}}